message: "If you use this software or its method, please cite it as below."
title: "Procedural Istanbul: origin–destination estimation from censored speed observations and an open traffic digital twin of Istanbul"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Aşıroğlu"
    given-names: "Abdurrahim Arif"
    email: "aaasiroglu@outlook.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/aaasiroglu/procedural-istanbul"
url: "https://aaasiroglu.github.io/procedural-istanbul/"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-10-21"
keywords:
  - traffic
  - digital twin
  - origin-destination estimation
  - inverse problem
  - SUMO
  - Istanbul
  - open data
  - Three.js
abstract: >-
  A browser-based 3D digital twin of Istanbul's Maslak – 15 July Bridge corridor built from open data, with a transport
  model that estimates origin–destination demand from İBB's live road speeds. Speeds enter as censored (one-sided)
  observations, every estimate reports its data share, the level of demand has its own identification measure, and
  validation uses held-out counts only. A shadow simulation forks SUMO's state at an incident to compare responses.
references:
